# Built for Shopify & App Store Review Standards

## 1. Polaris UI & Design Standards (React first)

This embedded admin app uses **`@shopify/polaris` React** as the default UI. Reference [Polaris React Storybook](https://storybook.polaris.shopify.dev/).

- Page wrapper: `<Page title="..." backAction={...} primaryAction={...}>`
- Columns: `<Layout><Layout.Section>...</Layout.Section></Layout>`
- Layout & stacks: `<BlockStack gap="400">`, `<InlineStack align="space-between" blockAlign="center">`
- Content & actions: `<Card>`, `<Text>`, `<Button>`, `<TextField>`, `<Banner>`, `<Badge>`
- Prefer Polaris primitives over raw HTML. Raw HTML/`div`/`button` is allowed only for editor chrome, drag handles, or when Polaris has no equivalent (`RangeSlider` for 0–100% size).
- **Do not** build new merchant screens entirely with Polaris Web Components (`s-page`, `s-stack`, `s-text-field`).

### Loading & empty states (required for App Store review)

- Every table or list MUST implement an `<EmptyState>` when no data exists.
- Every mutation must reflect loading feedback via `<Button loading={...}>` or Polaris `<Spinner>`.
- When loading data asynchronously, wrap views in `<SkeletonPage>` and `<SkeletonBodyText>`.

### Page shell

Use React Polaris `Page`: `title`, `backAction`, `primaryAction`, `secondaryActions`. Put the subtitle in the page body as `Text`.

## 2. App Bridge v4 Standards

Top-level merchant alerts and feedback must use `@shopify/app-bridge-react`:

```typescript
import { useAppBridge } from "@shopify/app-bridge-react";
const shopify = useAppBridge();
shopify.toast.show("Changes saved successfully");
```
